sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant S as Scheduler thread (replica A)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (pre_timer, pre_token)
  participant AD as Host adapter (AgentAdapter or ServiceAdapter)
  participant X as External agent or service

  rect rgb(230, 242, 241)
    Note over S,DB: TX1: claim with lease (target under 5 ms)
    S->>DB: SELECT ... FROM pre_timer WHERE next_fire_at <= now AND (locked_until IS NULL OR locked_until < now) FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
    S->>DB: UPDATE status=CLAIMED, locked_by=A, locked_until=now+60s, attempt+1
    S->>DB: COMMIT
  end

  Note over S,X: Outside any transaction: no DB connection, no row lock
  S->>AD: execute(invocation, attemptId, timeout)
  AD->>X: HTTP or MCP call (bounded by timeout)
  X-->>AD: structured output, or timeout
  AD-->>S: result or failure

  rect rgb(230, 242, 241)
    Note over S,DB: TX2: complete or fail (fresh transaction)
    S->>DB: SELECT ... FROM pre_timer WHERE id=? AND locked_by=A AND locked_until > now FOR UPDATE
    alt lease still held by A
      alt output valid and guardrail allows
        S->>DB: write pre_history, advance token, mark job DONE
      else guardrail route-to-human
        S->>DB: create approval pre_task with output and matched rules
      else failure, attempt < max
        S->>DB: status=DUE, next_fire_at=now+backoff, unlock
      else failure, attempts exhausted
        S->>DB: open pre_incident, token paused (or start compensation)
      end
      S->>DB: COMMIT
    else lease expired or taken by replica B
      S->>DB: ROLLBACK (result discarded, B's attempt owns the step)
    end
  end
